  (control (property_id "exact-address") (value 0) (reason "Only boundary 23 x15 expectation changes from 1 to 0, what an eight-byte reservation set would pair.") (id "eight-byte-set")
    (statement "Predeclared target: a set wider than the reservation must diverge."))
  (limitation "24 finite predeclared witnesses. exact width is past the reference: the pinned binary pairs an SC of another width at the same address, so it is a selection this case states and does not compare; the address and width a cleared reservation keeps have no effect while validity is clear, so nothing here observes them; no other hart or device exists here to invalidate anything; only the cleared validity of the reset state is observable; this selects one laboratory realization and claims nothing of multicore behaviour")
  (source_id "RVI-A") (source_locator "12.1.2") (category "implementation-defined") (risk "medium")
  (coverage "24 witnesses: no reservation at reset, exactly the LR's word, both widths, LR replacing, SC invalidating either way, each target fault keeping it, aliases, and six ordinary instructions preserving it")
